meta {
  name: Post Create Inventory
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/inventory
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

body:multipart-form {
  vehicle_id: e1288783-a5d4-1c4c-2cd6-0e92f7cc3bf9
  inventory_name: Secondary Tire
  inventory_category: Vehicle Component
  inventory_storage: Trunk
  inventory_qty: 1
  inventory_image_url: @file()
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Post Create Inventory

  This request is used to create an inventory by using given `vehicle_id`, `inventory_name`, `inventory_category`, `inventory_storage`, `inventory_qty`, and `inventory_image_url`. This request interacts with the MySQL database, firebase storage, has a protected routes, and audited activity (history).

  ## Request Body (multipart/form-data)

  | Field                | Type    | Required | Description               |
  |------------------------|---------|----------|-----------------------------|
  | vehicle_id            | string  | yes      | Vehicle ID                 |
  | inventory_name        | string  | yes      | Inventory name              |
  | inventory_category    | string  | yes      | Inventory category          |
  | inventory_storage     | string  | yes      | Inventory storage location  |
  | inventory_qty         | integer | yes      | Quantity                    |
  | inventory_image_url   | file    | no       | Inventory image (binary)    |

  ## Responses

  **201 — inventory created**
```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "inventory created"
  }
```

  **400 — inventory failed to validated**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "[failed validation message]"
  }
```

  **401 — protected route need to include sign in token as authorization bearer**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "you need to include the authorization token from login"
  }
```

  **500 — Internal Server Error**
```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "something wrong. please contact admin"
  }
```
}